        "original_id": "b9c7dafb-6766-5403-8483-7a2d08227b96",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Operation Grenade, Lorraine Campaign, Operation Clarion\n- Organizations: U.S. Ninth Army, U.S. Third Army, Allied forces\n- People: Lieutenant General William Hood Simpson\n- Places: Roer (Rur) river, Roermond, Düren, Lorraine, Germany\n- Topics: World War II, strategic bombing\n\nFacts:\n- From September 1, 1944, through December 18, 1944, the Lorraine Campaign was the term used by U.S. Army historians for operations of the U.S. Third Army in Lorraine during World War II.\n- In February 1945, Operation Grenade was the U.S. Ninth Army crossing of the Roer (Rur) river between Roermond and Düren during World War II.\n- Lieutenant General William Hood Simpson commanded the U.S. Ninth Army during Operation Grenade.\n- Operation Clarion was an extensive Allied strategic bombing campaign during World War II.\n- Operation Clarion attacked 200 German communication network targets to open Operation Veritable/Grenade.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
